IMPORT prelude

-- Voluntary Sterilisation Act 1974 (Singapore) -- what counts as treatment for sexual sterilisation (s 2), who must consent and when
-- a court order is needed (s 3(2)), the explanation and certification (s 3(3)), where and by whom it may be done (s 4), secrecy
-- (s 5), coercion (s 7), the doctor's immunity (s 8), conscientious objection (s 10), and the three offences and their maximum
-- penalties (ss 3(5), 5(2), 7).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 5/12/2025"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/VSA1974.txt. The latest amendment annotated is Act 19 of 2025 wef 05/12/2025 (the definitions of
-- "health institution" and "specialist medical clinic" in s 2); s 13(2)(a) is annotated Act 11 of 2023 wef 01/05/2023. The
-- arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is out of step by one line with the body; this row follows the body's numbers.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance to ordinary people in Singapore (Tier 1): anyone considering a vasectomy or
-- tubal ligation, the parents of a young unmarried adult, and the families of a person who lacks mental capacity meet it. SCOPED to
-- the whole operative Act, which is short. Not encoded: s 6 (inspection powers), s 9 (not grievous hurt under Penal Code s 320 --
-- declaratory, recorded in a comment only), s 13 (regulations), the Mental Capacity Act 2008 tests that s 3(4) imports (capacity and
-- best interests are taken as given facts), the "prescribed" disclosure exceptions and surgical qualifications (no regulations were
-- retrieved), and which acute-hospital or ambulatory-surgical licences a premises holds under the Healthcare Services Act 2020.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the example naive rows. No pipeline, no coverage
-- table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Voluntary Sterilisation Act 1974`

§§ `2 -- treatment for sexual sterilisation`

-- s 2: "treatment for sexual sterilisation" means "the surgical sterilisation of a male or female that does not involve removal of
-- the reproduction glands or organs unless the removal is necessary for medical or therapeutic reasons."
GIVEN `surgical` IS A BOOLEAN, `removes the reproductive glands or organs` IS A BOOLEAN, `the removal is medically or therapeutically necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the procedure is treatment for sexual sterilisation` IF
        `surgical`
    AND (    (NOT `removes the reproductive glands or organs`)
         OR  `the removal is medically or therapeutically necessary`)

§§ `3(2) -- consent and court orders`

-- s 3(2): a registered medical practitioner may carry out the treatment "if, and only if":
--   (a) married or unmarried, 21 or older -- "if the person consents";
--   (b) married, below 21 -- "if the person consents";
--   (c) unmarried, below 21 -- "if the person, and at least one parent or guardian of the person, both consent";
--   (d) married and lacking capacity (Mental Capacity Act 2008 s 4) -- "if, on the application of the person's spouse, the court
--       makes an order declaring that the treatment is necessary in the best interests of that person";
--   (e) unmarried and lacking capacity -- the same, "on the application of at least one parent or guardian".
-- (a) is "subject to paragraphs (d) and (e)", (b) to (d), (c) to (e): capacity is tested first.
-- s 2: "court" means "the General Division of the High Court or a Family Court".
DECLARE Patient HAS
    `age` IS A NUMBER
    `married` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lacks capacity to consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consents` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a parent or guardian consents` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a court has declared it necessary in their best interests` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court application was by the spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court application was by a parent or guardian` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the patient` IS A Patient
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a court order is the route` IF
    `the patient`'s `lacks capacity to consent`

GIVEN `the patient` IS A Patient
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a parent's consent is also needed` IF
        (NOT `the patient`'s `lacks capacity to consent`)
    AND (NOT `the patient`'s `married`)
    AND `the patient`'s `age` < 21

GIVEN `the patient` IS A Patient
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 3(2) conditions are satisfied` IF
        (    `the patient`'s `lacks capacity to consent`
         AND `the patient`'s `a court has declared it necessary in their best interests`
         AND (    (`the patient`'s `married` AND `the patient`'s `the court application was by the spouse`)
              OR  ((NOT `the patient`'s `married`) AND `the patient`'s `the court application was by a parent or guardian`)))
    OR  (    (NOT `the patient`'s `lacks capacity to consent`)
         AND `the patient`'s `consents`
         AND (    (NOT `a parent's consent is also needed` `the patient`)
              OR  `the patient`'s `a parent or guardian consents`))

§§ `3(3) -- explanation and certification`

-- s 3(3): before treatment the practitioner "must give to the person undergoing the treatment, not being a person who lacks capacity
-- ... a full and reasonable explanation as to the meaning and consequences of that treatment, and that person must certify that he or
-- she clearly understands". This is not one of the s 3(2) conditions, and s 3(5) punishes only a failure of the s 3(2) conditions.
GIVEN `lacks capacity` IS A BOOLEAN, `explained fully and reasonably` IS A BOOLEAN, `certified understanding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 3(3) requirement is met` IF
        `lacks capacity`
    OR  (`explained fully and reasonably` AND `certified understanding`)

§§ `4 -- where and by whom`

-- s 4(1): "every treatment for sexual sterilisation must only be carried out -- (a) in a health institution; and (b) by a registered
-- medical practitioner who is authorised, by the person having the management or control of the health institution".
-- (2): in a specialist medical clinic the practitioner "must also possess the prescribed surgical or obstetric qualifications".
-- s 2: "health institution" means premises licensed under the Healthcare Services Act 2020 for "an acute hospital service or
-- ambulatory surgical centre service", or "any specialist medical clinic" (an outpatient-licensed premises employing or engaging a
-- specialist registered under Medical Registration Act 1997 s 22 in a prescribed branch).
-- The Act attaches no penalty to s 4 and has no general penalty section.
DECLARE Premises IS ONE OF
    `an acute hospital`
    `an ambulatory surgical centre`
    `a specialist medical clinic`
    `a general practitioner's clinic`

GIVEN `the premises` IS A Premises
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the premises is a health institution` IF
    CONSIDER `the premises`
    WHEN `a general practitioner's clinic` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the premises` IS A Premises, `authorised by the management` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds the prescribed qualifications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 4 place and practitioner rules are met` IF
        `the premises is a health institution` `the premises`
    AND `authorised by the management`
    AND (    (NOT (`the premises` EQUALS `a specialist medical clinic`))
         OR  `holds the prescribed qualifications`)

§§ `5 -- secrecy`

-- s 5(1): a person concerned with keeping the medical records, or who participates in the treatment, "must not, unless the person
-- upon whom the treatment has been performed expressly consents to the disclosure, disclose any facts or information relating to that
-- treatment except to such persons and for such purposes as may be prescribed." (2): fine up to $10,000, prison up to 12 months, or
-- both.
GIVEN `kept the records or took part` IS A BOOLEAN, `disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the patient expressly consented` IS A BOOLEAN, `to a prescribed person for a prescribed purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence` IF
        `kept the records or took part`
    AND `disclosed`
    AND (NOT `the patient expressly consented`)
    AND (NOT `to a prescribed person for a prescribed purpose`)

§§ `7 -- coercion`

-- s 7: "Any person who, by means of coercion or intimidation, compels or induces another person to undergo treatment for sexual
-- sterilisation against that other person's will" commits an offence: fine up to $10,000, prison up to 5 years, or both.
GIVEN `used coercion or intimidation` IS A BOOLEAN, `against the other person's will` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the inducement is an offence` IF
    `used coercion or intimidation` AND `against the other person's will`

§§ `3(5), 5(2), 7 -- maximum penalties`

-- s 3(5): a practitioner who operates "when the requisite conditions referred to in subsection (2) ... are not satisfied" -- fine up
-- to $10,000, prison up to 5 years, or both. s 5(2): $10,000 or 12 months. s 7: $10,000 or 5 years.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `operating without the s 3(2) conditions`
    `unauthorised disclosure`
    `coercing sterilisation`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unauthorised disclosure` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 60

GIVEN `the patient` IS A Patient
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `operating is an s 3(5) offence` IF
    NOT `the s 3(2) conditions are satisfied` `the patient`

§§ `8, 9 -- immunity`

-- s 8: "No registered medical practitioner shall be liable civilly or criminally for carrying out treatment for sexual sterilisation
-- on any person so long as -- (a) the conditions in section 3(2) are satisfied in respect of that person; and (b) the treatment is
-- not carried out in a negligent manner." Neither s 3(3) nor s 4 is a condition of the immunity.
-- s 9: "any treatment for sexual sterilisation by a registered medical practitioner does not constitute grievous hurt under section
-- 320 of the Penal Code 1871" (not encoded as a rule).
GIVEN `the patient` IS A Patient, `negligent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the practitioner is immune` IF
    `the s 3(2) conditions are satisfied` `the patient` AND (NOT `negligent`)

§§ `10 -- conscientious objection`

-- s 10: "No person is under any duty, whether by contract or by any statutory or legal requirement, to participate in any treatment
-- for sexual sterilisation authorised by this Act to which the person has a conscientious objection." No exception (for example for
-- an emergency) is written in.
GIVEN `has a conscientious objection` IS A BOOLEAN, `a contract requires participation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a duty to participate` IF
    `a contract requires participation` AND (NOT `has a conscientious objection`)
